<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - S.AFRICA JUNE PPI UP 7.5 PCT Y/Y.</title>
<headline>TABLE - S.AFRICA JUNE PPI UP 7.5 PCT Y/Y.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-commodities</p>
<p>producer price index fell 0.2 percent in June from May after</p>
<p>rising 0.9 percent in May, Central Statistical Service figures</p>
<p>show.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise in June was 7.5 percent after May's</p>
<p>8.4 percent rise.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast PPI would</p>
<p>rise 0.5 percent month-on-month and 8.3 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>    Pct changes:	     Year/year		    month/month</p>
<p>			 Jun'97   May'97   Jun'96	latest   prev</p>
<p>All commodities    7.5	8.4	6.1	   -0.2	0.9</p>
<p>Locally produced   8.5	8.9	6.5	    0.2	0.4</p>
<p>Imported	     4.1	6.4	4.7	   -1.4	2.7</p>
<p>Index (base 1995=100):</p>
<p>			 Jun'97    May'97    Jun'96</p>
<p>All commodities    114.1     114.3     106.1</p>
<p>Locally produced   115.6     115.4     106.5</p>
<p>Imported	     109.0     110.5     104.7</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
